ef name trusts a re-created branch (pre-existing).\nRationale: The diff changes what the gate admits, so the gate read every new admission path. Without --base-ref every path defaults to the latest answer's base, so behaviour is unchanged. With it, a foreign-base answer admits only on an unchanged merge base or an equal non-empty range patch-id. That is the same range, so a squash landing cannot slip through. Strongest remaining attack: --base-ref is caller-supplied, and a wrong base could still pass if it shares the answer's merge base. That admits only an identical range. It is not a widening.\n","forge_read":"2026-11-13T13:09:09Z"}
